<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Karkota dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">625 CE – 855 CE (approx.) · capital Parihaspora</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The dynasty that made Kashmir a regional empire under Lalitaditya Muktapida and built the Sun temple at Martand.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajatarangini">Kalhana's Rajatarangini</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durlabhavardhana">Durlabhavardhana</a> founded the dynasty around 625, succeeding the last king of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gonanda-dynasty">Gonanda dynasty</a> through marriage. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuanzang">Xuanzang</a> visited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> during his reign and described a powerful kingdom with many Buddhist monasteries.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitaditya-muktapida">Lalitaditya Muktapida</a>, who ruled in the 8th century, led campaigns into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> and beyond, defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yashovarman-of-kannauj">Yashovarman</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/varman-dynasty-of-kannauj">Varman dynasty of Kannauj</a>, and sent envoys to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a>. He founded the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parihaspora">Parihaspora</a> and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martand-sun-temple">Martand Sun temple</a>, whose ruins still dominate the valley. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> became a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> poetry and philosophy, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayapida">Jayapida</a> later patronised scholars and poets at his court. Irrigation and saffron supported the economy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Later Karkota kings were weak and dominated by ministers and court factions. In 855 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avantivarman">Avantivarman</a> took the throne, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/utpala-dynasty">Utpala dynasty</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 625 CE – 855 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:72.14%;width:4.58%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>625 CE – 855 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Parihaspora</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Durlabhavardhana, Lalitaditya Muktapida, Jayapida</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a>, <a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Karkota Empire, Karkotas of Kashmir</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=740&amp;focus=karkota-dynasty" aria-label="Karkota dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6585 942 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Karkota dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6905 1198L7103 1442M6905 1198L6912 1204M6905 1198L6905 1198"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7103 1442h0M6912 1204h0M6905 1198h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6905 1198h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6905 1198h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=740&amp;focus=karkota-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
